The Village Sarpanch
 
Sixteen-year-old Lakshmi questioned why no women attended village meetings. When told, "it's not their place," she started a girls' discussion group in her school.

They learned about women's rights and village governance. With her teacher's help, Lakshmi organized cleanliness drives and literacy campaigns.

Years later, she became the youngest female Sarpanch (Village head) in her district. Now, half the seats at village meetings are filled with women. "Change begins with questioning unfair traditions," she tells young girls.